# ── CodeFreedom — Trivy ignore list ────────────────────────────────────────
# Use only for vulnerabilities that have NO upstream fix at scan time AND
# whose affected code path is unreachable in our build/runtime context.
# Each entry MUST be reviewed when a fixed version ships upstream.
#
# Trivy syntax:  CVE-YYYY-NNNN  [exp:YYYY-MM-DD]
# The `exp:` directive is a self-imposed review deadline, not a Trivy
# enforcement. Trivy will suppress the finding until the date passes.
#
# Last reviewed: 2026-06-05
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── python:3.13-slim (Dockerfile.Web, Dockerfile.Bridge) ─────────────────
# Affected package: libncursesw6 (ncurses). The Bridge and the Camoufox
# service are non-interactive HTTP daemons; ncurses is only loaded by
# terminal-driven CLIs which we do not exec. No code path is exposed.
CVE-2025-69720  exp:2026-12-31

# Affected package: perl-base. Perl is not installed by any of our
# Dockerfiles and the Bridge/Camoufox services never exec a Perl
# interpreter. perl-base is pulled into the slim Debian base as a
# transitive dependency of dpkg/apt, but it is dormant at runtime.
# The five entries below cover all current critical/high perl CVEs
# flagged in python:3.13-slim at scan time. Re-check after 5.40.1-7.
CVE-2026-42496  exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-8376   exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-42497  exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-48962  exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-9538   exp:2026-12-31
